Third-party components
----------------------

my-pdf-tools includes or loads the components below, each under its own license.
The license texts shipped with the program are in the `licenses/` folder.

  PDFium (the PDF reading engine, loaded as pdfium.dll / libpdfium.dylib)
      BSD-3-Clause. Prebuilt binaries from bblanchon/pdfium-binaries (MIT).
      Texts: licenses/PDFium-LICENSE.txt and licenses/pdfium-third-party/.

  Typst (typst, typst-pdf, typst-layout) -- PDF typesetting engine
      Apache-2.0.

  typst-assets and the fonts it bundles (Libertinus Serif, New Computer Modern,
  DejaVu Sans Mono, and others)
      Apache-2.0 for the crate; SIL Open Font License 1.1 and the DejaVu font
      license for the fonts. Texts: licenses/typst-assets-LICENSE.txt and
      licenses/typst-assets-NOTICE.txt.

  Tauri 2, tauri-plugin-dialog              Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  rfd (native file dialogs, used by the plugin)
                                            MIT
  pdfium-render, serde, serde_json,
  thiserror, image                          MIT OR Apache-2.0
  pulldown-cmark, ts-rs                     MIT
  unicode-normalization                     (MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND Unicode-3.0
  React and the other npm dependencies      MIT (see package-lock.json)

This list covers the direct dependencies. The complete list, with the license text of
every transitive dependency, will be generated for the release builds.
